---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import LangSwitch from '../../../components/LangSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of use of the Dominoland app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="Terms of use of the Dominoland mobile game: a free game with no ads, no purchases and no account, progress on the phone, intellectual property, liability, governing law."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/dominoland/cgu/', en: '/en/dominoland/cgu/', es: '/es/dominoland/cgu/', de: '/de/dominoland/cgu/', it: '/it/dominoland/cgu/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<div class="stack gap-8">
			<LangSwitch
				lang="en"
				links={[
					{ lang: 'fr', href: '/dominoland/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'es', href: '/es/dominoland/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'de', href: '/de/dominoland/cgu/' },
					{ lang: 'it', href: '/it/dominoland/cgu/' },
				]}
			/>
			<Hero
				title="Terms of use — Dominoland"
				tagline="A free game, with no ads and no purchases."
			/>
		</div>

		<p class="updated">
			<strong>Dominoland</strong> app (<code>com.ludivenstudio.dominoland</code>) — last updated: November 26, 2026.
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the <a href="/dominoland/cgu/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>Key points before you play:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>The game is a <strong>free</strong> download. It has <strong>no ads, no in-app purchases and no subscription</strong>.</li>
				<li>It plays <strong>with no account and no network</strong>: your progress stays on your phone.</li>
				<li>Stars and best scores <strong>have no cash value</strong>.</li>
				<li>The game is for everyone, aged <strong>13 and up</strong>. It has <strong>no online play and no chat</strong>.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Purpose and acceptance</h2>
			<p>These terms govern the use of the Dominoland mobile game (hereinafter "the Game"). By installing or using the Game, you accept them. If you refuse them, do not use the Game and uninstall it.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Publisher</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Company name: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with share capital of €1,000</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>EU VAT number: FR20&nbsp;999253586</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Publication director: Ludiven Studio</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. The Game</h2>
			<p>Dominoland is a puzzle and rhythm game: you draw lines of dominoes, start the wave, and the fallen pieces make a picture. It has three modes: The Trace, Rhythm and the Endless path.</p>
			<p>The Game is free. It shows no ads and sells nothing: no content is paid.</p>
			<p>Playing needs no account and no network. When your phone is online, the Game checks at launch for a newer version and sends usage statistics with no ID (see the <a href="/en/dominoland/confidentialite/">privacy policy</a>). Connection and equipment costs are yours.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. Your progress</h2>
			<p>Your progress (levels, stars, best scores) is kept <strong>on your phone only</strong>. You can lose it by uninstalling the Game or changing phones, unless your phone's backup restores it. As the Game has no account, the publisher has no copy of it and cannot give it back.</p>
			<p>Stars and best scores are a <strong>personal licence of use</strong> within the Game. They <strong>have no cash value</strong>: they cannot be turned into money, traded or resold.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>The Game, its code, its levels, its images, its animations, its sounds, its music and its texts belong to Ludiven Studio or its licensors and are protected by intellectual property law. You receive a personal, non-exclusive right of use. Components by other authors remain their authors', under their licenses, listed in the Game (Options › "Credits and licences") and in the <a href="/mentions-legales/#licences-dominoland">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. Changes, interruption and discontinuation of the service</h2>
			<p>The publisher may change the Game, add or remove features and levels. Should a future version add ads or purchases, these terms and the privacy policy would be updated first, and the date at the top of the page would change.</p>
			<p>The publisher may stop all or part of the service, in particular if a store requires its removal. The levels will stay playable as long as the installed version works on your phone.</p>
			<p>These terms may change. The date of the last update is at the top of the page. If there is a major change, we will let you know; playing on means you accept it.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. Liability</h2>
			<p>The Game is provided as is. The publisher does not guarantee that it works without interruption or error on all phones.</p>
			<p>The publisher can only be held liable in the event of proven fault, and its liability is limited to direct and foreseeable damage. It does not cover the loss of progress kept on the phone. Nothing here excludes its liability in the event of gross negligence or physical injury, nor limits your mandatory consumer rights.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. Personal data</h2>
			<p>The processing of your data is described in the <a href="/en/dominoland/confidentialite/">Dominoland privacy policy</a>, which is part of these terms.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. Governing law and disputes</h2>
			<p>These terms are governed by <strong>French law</strong>. If you are a consumer living in another member state of the European Union, you keep the mandatory protections of your country.</p>
			{/* TODO legal: replace with the mediator's name, address and website once adhesion is signed (art. L612-1). */}
			<p>If there is a problem, write to us first: we will look for an amicable solution. If there is no solution within one month, you can turn to a consumer mediator free of charge (Article L612-1 of the French Consumer Code). The mediator's contact details are given on request at <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. Failing agreement, the dispute will be brought before the competent courts.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Contact</h2>
			<p>For any question or to report a problem: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--sc-ink-2);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--sc-ink);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--sc-link);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--sc-muted);
	}
	.summary {
		border: 1px solid var(--sc-line);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--sc-accent);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--sc-surface);
	}
	.summary p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--sc-surface);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
	}
</style>
